          "1a": "Multi-national self-controlled case series (SCCS).",
          "3": "Among " + (s.picoP || "(population)") + ", does " + (s.picoI || "(exposure)") + " change the rate of " + (s.picoO || "(outcome)") + "? Estimated within-person.",
          "4": "Self-controlled case series. Each case acts as their own control, so all time-invariant between-person confounding is removed by design.",
          // This used to end "Observation, exposure-risk and pre-exposure
          // windows as defined in the protocol" whatever the strip contained —
          // so a protocol carrying the outstanding issue "No pre-exposure risk
          // window" still told STROBE item 5 that its pre-exposure windows were
          // defined. Name the segments that are actually there.
          "5": "AsPEN sites: " + sitesPlain + ". Study period: " + (s.studyCalendar || "(not specified)") + ". Observation period: " +
               (({ "age-cohort": "later of the calendar start of the study period or cohort entry age", "study-start": "calendar start of the study period", "age-onset": "age at first eligibility", enrolment: "date of database registration" })[s.obsStart] || "(not specified)") + " to " +
               (({ "earliest-of": "the earliest of end of study period, death or disenrolment", "study-end": "the calendar end of the study period", death: "death", disenrol: "disenrolment from the database" })[s.obsEnd] || "(not specified)") + ". Period strip: " +
               (parsePeriods(s.periods).map((p) => p.name + " " + rowDays(p)).join(" → ") || "(not defined)") + ".",
          "6": "Cases experiencing the outcome during the observation period. Case definition: " + (s.outcomeDef || "(case definition)") + " (" + (s.outcomeCodes || "codes TBD") + "). Event handling: " + (s.eventHandling === "first" ? "first event only" : "all events (recurrent)") + ".",
          "7": "Exposure: " + (s.picoI || s.exposureName || "(exposure)") + ". Outcome: " + (s.picoO || "(outcome)") + " (" + (s.outcomeCodes || "codes TBD") + "). Time-varying covariates:\n" + bul(tvc),
          "8": "Routinely-collected health data from the contributing databases (" + sitesPlain + "). Outcomes ascertained by the code set " + (s.outcomeCodes || "(codes)") + ".",
          "9": "The self-controlled design removes all fixed between-person confounders. Residual (time-varying) bias addressed by pre-specified sensitivity analyses:\n" + bul(sens),
          "11": "Age modelled as a time-varying covariate in " + ageTxt + " bands; seasonality: " + seasonTxt + ".",
          // Item 11 above reports the season setting the user chose; this item
          // used to assert "with age and season as time-varying covariates"
          // regardless, so with season set to None the two adjacent rows of one
          // table contradicted each other. It also named a conditional Poisson
          // model even when section 10's primary model said otherwise.
          "12": (s.primaryModel || "Conditional Poisson regression with offset for log person-time") + " for the within-person " + (s.effectMeasure || "incidence rate ratio (IRR)") +
                ". Age modelled as a time-varying covariate in " + ageTxt + " bands; seasonality: " + seasonTxt +
                ". Site-specific estimates pooled by " + metaTxt + " meta-analysis (report I², τ²). Subgroups:\n" + bul(subg) + "\nSensitivity analyses:\n" + bul(sens),
          "17": "Pre-specified subgroups:\n" + bul(subg) + "\nSensitivity analyses:\n" + bul(sens),
